
AlphaDict 1.5 (unreleased):
        -- configure is rewritten around pkg-config: Qt is located with
           pkg-config only, no include or library path is hard-coded, Qt 5.9 or
           newer is required, and Qt6 is detected up front and rejected with an
           explanation instead of failing deep inside the build.
        -- The GUI sources are ported to Qt5: translation strings regenerated
           (lupdate/lrelease), Qt5 signal/slot syntax, QRegExp/QTextCodec and
           QDesktopWidget usage replaced.
        -- New QML user interface (CONFIG_QML): rounded cards, themed sidebar,
           custom scroll bars, light and dark colour schemes. Build it with
           --enable-qml; --disable-qml keeps the legacy QtWidgets interface.
        -- The QML window has no system title bar: minimise, close and drag
           are drawn by the application. The default font size is 20 and the
           sidebar buttons are square, so the text fills most of the button.
        -- AlphaDict now runs as a single instance. Starting it again while a
           copy is running raises the existing window instead of asking to
           start another process.
        -- Closing the window hides it to the system tray when "system tray"
           is enabled in the settings (the default); the tray icon brings the
           window back. Disable the option to close the program on close.
        -- Screen word capture uses plain Xlib instead of Qt5X11Extras.
        -- Dictionary directory scanning accepts *.aldict only (case
           insensitive), so stray xml files and editor backups no longer show
           up as dictionaries.
        -- The built-in help (help.cn/help.en) is HTML now: headings, lists and
           clickable links rendered with the theme font and accent colour.
        -- Dictionaries are installed as data: every *.aldict in system/dicts/
           is copied to <datadir>/dicts by 'make install', and 'make clean' no
           longer touches the dictionary directory. No sample dictionary is
           generated at build time any more.
        -- aldctl is built into src/tools and installed to both <bindir> and
           <datadir>/tools, so that directory works on its own.
        -- The four *_to_aldtxt.py converters and lib_aldict.py are merged into
           tools/aldconv.py: one script, format auto-detection (-f to force),
           and StarDict 64-bit offsets supported.
        -- The dictionary front-end is plain text only: the XML reader and the
           old *_to_aldictxml.py tools were removed. 'aldctl build' turns text
           into a .aldict, 'aldctl export' writes any dictionary back to text
           for editing; doc/make_dictionary.txt explains the workflow.
        -- Memory handling fixes throughout the dictionary and GUI layers:
           leaked index items in the prefix-search and sizing paths, a leaked
           worker QThread in QtMessager, a stale file handle in the
           AldictDocument constructor, a double free of the cached index
           'opaque' pointer, and an off-by-one overread in ReadFile.
        -- Vocabulary book exam mode keeps its answer flags in sync with the
           word list, so adding or removing a row no longer shifts the results.
        -- Build output is no longer kept in the tree: the VS2013/VS2015
           directories (stale Qt5.3 project files, checked-in Release binaries
           and DLLs, IDE user state) are removed, and generated uic/moc/rcc
           output and *.qm files are ignored. configure + make rebuilds them.
        -- The runtime data directory moved out of the sources: src/system is
           now the top-level system/ (dictionaries stay in system/dicts), and
           the unused design drawings (doc/*.dia) and GIMP sources (resource/)
           have been dropped. A Debian packaging directory (debian/) ships the
           programs, a desktop entry and the dictionaries; README.en is reduced
           to the project URL.

AlphaDict 1.2:
        -- Support Screen Translation (take a word from screen and translate).
        -- System Tray.

AlphaDict 1.1
	-- Release windows version.
	-- Added vocubulary book.
        -- Support dictionaries of "IDP" and "dicts.info".

AlphaDict 1.0
	The first version: basically lookup, support cedict and stardict dictionaries
	by using tools to convert.

AlConvert 1.0
	The first version: support "Front-end format of alphadict v1" and
        "File Structure of Alphadict Dictionary Version 1".
	
	Support duplicate index, eg: the same index string within in the tree,
	with different explantion. This is a unpleasant feature, for supporting cedict.

